title: "Collatz basin densities and affine Fourier decay: papers and Lean proofs"
authors:
  - family-names: Valbuena
    given-names: Lucas
repository-code: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
url: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
abstract: >-
  Two papers with Lean proofs. The affine-law paper proves primitive Fourier
  decay uniform in a growing conductor deficit and in the affine seed, with
  conditional decay on polynomial-mass total-exponent slices and the exact
  central slice. The basin paper proves uniform inverse-linear predecessor
  density bounds, a finite cylinder-energy criterion for universal eventual
  periodicity, a raw occupation lower bound and divergent-component excess,
  and an almost-sure inverse height clock. The repository includes source
  proofs, pinned dependencies, verification records, and attribution.
  A matching raw occupation upper bound and the Collatz conjecture remain open.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - predecessor density
  - natural density
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - canonical traces
  - Fourier decay
  - Syracuse affine laws
  - Subspace Theorem
